* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-takeoff.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[rising]] or [[ascent]] of an [[aircraft]] or [[rocket]] into [[flight]].
#: {{uxi|en|The flight was smooth, but the '''takeoff''' was a little rough.}}
#: {{cot|en|landing}}
# A [[parody]] or [[lampoon]] of someone or something.
#: {{ux|en|{{w|Weird Al Yankovic|Weird Al}}'s song "Lasagna" is a '''takeoff''' on the popular song "La Bamba".}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1897|author=Edward Bellamy|title=Equality|chapter=[[s:Equality (Bellamy)/Chapter 23|ch. 23]]
|passage=I came across a little pamphlet of the period, yellow and almost undecipherable, which, on examination, I found to be a rather amusing skit or satirical '''take-off''' on the profit system.}}
# A [[quantification]], especially of [[building]] [[material]]s.
#: {{uxi|en|I'll give you an estimate after I do the quantity '''takeoffs''' for the trusses and structural steel.}}
# {{lb|en|printing|UK|historical}} The [[removal]] of [[sheet]]s from the [[press]].
# The spot from which one [[take off|takes off]]; specifically, the place from which a [[jumper]] [[rise]]s in [[leap]]ing.
#* ''Encyclopaedia of Sport''
#*: The '''take-off''' should be selected with great care, and a pit of large dimensions provided on the landing side.

